          "kicker": "FUNDING CRISIS",
          "heading": "Manager Lionel Danford appeals for funds to save deaf sevens campaign",
          "body": "The Fiji men’s and women’s deaf rugby sevens teams are facing a major financial hurdle ahead of the upcoming World Deaf Rugby Sevens Championship in Tokyo. Team manager Lionel Danford revealed a funding gap of up to $70,000 remains for daily expenses and camp preparations, despite valuable kit sponsorship from PacificAus Sports. Many of the squad's players are currently unemployed and must cover their own transport costs to Sigatoka. Despite these hardships, preparations continue, including a crucial scrimmage session scheduled against Osea Kolinisau’s national sevens side."
